walaOS is a 64-bit RISC V operating system.

Done:
- Kernel boot
- Serial console and logging
- RISC V traps and interrupts
- Physical and virtual memory management
- Kernel heap allocation

To do:
- Add a scheduler
- Add user programs and processes
- Add a filesystem
- Add more hardware drivers
- Add networking
- Add a shell
- Add gigapage and megapage support
- Refactor and clean up the kernel
